  "result": "Excellent! All 128 tests pass (including 18 new payment tests). Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**src/payments.js** \u2014 New module with three functions:\n\n- **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an issued or partially_paid invoice. Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with the payment added to `invoice.payments`. Updates status to `'paid'` when fully paid, or `'partially_paid'` while something is owed. Validates:\n  - **NOT_ISSUED**: status must be 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n  - **AMOUNT_INVALID**: amount must be a positive integer\n  - **OVERPAYMENT**: payment can't exceed balance due\n\n- **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Returns the total owed minus what's been paid\n\n- **`totalPaid(invoice)`** \u2014 Helper that sums all payments on an invoice\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error codes:\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: for non-issuable invoices\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: for payments exceeding balance\n\n**test/payments.test.js** \u2014 18 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Recording single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- All error conditions\n- Balance calculations with and without discounts\n- Immutability verification",
